From 98285d348e43ef412d5aad89bec7d01f4e9928a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 08:45:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir_typeck: an inherent method call waits while its `Self` is an ivar

typed-path 0.12.3 src/common/utf8/path.rs:941-945 (fselect 0.10.3):

    let rw = Box::into_raw(self) as *mut str;
    let inner = unsafe { Box::from_raw(rw) };
    Utf8PathBuf { _encoding: PhantomData, inner: inner.into_string() }

    error: Failed to locate function <_>::into_string

The argument coercion `*mut str -> *mut T` for `Box::from_raw` is
still pending, so `inner` is `Box<_>` when `into_string` (alloc's
`impl str`, `self: Box<str>`) is looked up. The inherent search looks
through `Box<_>` for `self: Box<Self>` methods, matches `impl str`
against the ivar, and gives `<_>::into_string`.
visit_call_populate_cache then searched the impls of `_`, found none,
and failed hard. rustc wouldn't see an ivar here, since it unifies
argument coercions at once.

visit_call_populate_cache_UfcsInherent now returns "not yet" while the
path's `Self` is still an ivar, as it does for an ambiguous impl. The
call is looked up again once the coercion has set `T = str`. A `Self`
that never becomes known still ends in an error (spare rules), not a loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/src/hir_typeck/expr_cs__enum.cpp b/src/hir_typeck/expr_cs__enum.cpp
index a705f81f..1d52aece 100644
--- a/src/hir_typeck/expr_cs__enum.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_typeck/expr_cs__enum.cpp
@@ -401,6 +401,15 @@ namespace typecheck
     {
         auto& e = path.m_data.as_UfcsInherent();
 
+        // `Self` still unknown (an inherent method reached through a custom receiver's inner type, `self: Box<Self>` on
+        // `Box<_>`): no impl can be picked yet, so wait for the type
+        // - typed-path 0.12.3 common/utf8/path.rs:945: `let inner = Box::from_raw(rw); inner.into_string()` with
+        //   `rw: *mut str`, its coercion to `*mut T` still pending -> "Failed to locate function <_>::into_string"
+        if( context.get_type(e.type).data().is_Infer() ) {
+            DEBUG("- `Self` is still an ivar (" << e.type << "), waiting");
+            return false;
+        }
+
         const ::HIR::TypeImpl* impl_ptr = nullptr;
         // Detect multiple applicable methods and get the caller to try again later if there are multiple
         unsigned int count = 0;
